-              <p>The truncation term \(\tfrac12 M_2 h\) decreases as \(h\) falls, so it cannot produce the rise. The term \(2\delta/h\) grows as \(h\) falls and is the round-off term, which dominates at these steps. At \(h = 10^{-15}\) the two computed values agree in almost all digits, and Definition 4.1 bounds the quotient's round-off error by \(2\delta/h\). With the assumed \(\delta = 2.22 \times 10^{-16}\) of the Lab 1 discussion, that bound is \(0.444\) at \(h = 10^{-15}\), and the printed error \(0.390\) is consistent with it.</p>
